    "text": "While the study found that 54.1% of anemic children had iron deficiency anemia based on the MI > 13, this estimate may be inflated due to the inherent limitations of relying solely on this hematological ratio. The MI, calculated as MCV divided by RBC count, is a useful screening tool in resource-lim",
